<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Mackie 1996 pre-tax loss 0.44 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Mackie 1996 pre-tax loss 0.44 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million sterling unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		4.8 loss	     vs 30.5 profit</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 3.7		    vs 11.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     0.44 loss	    vs 3.27 profit</p>
<p> Turnover		   17.74		  vs 22.68</p>
<p>NOTE - Full company name - Mackie International Plc is a Northern-Irish based engineering company.</p>
<p>The group named Sul Sahota as group chief executive and said Peter Long had resigned as director and group chief executive.</p>
<p>Mackie said it made a loss after incurring exceptional charges of 1.9 million which relate to the restructuring of the textile operations and pension provisions.</p>
<p>The group recommended that no final dividend be paid which makes a total dividend of 3.7 pence per share for 1996 compared with 11.0 pence in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
